From a5d5c191ebde1b4b610497387e8ca4b82be24ae7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:55:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 48/49] [GBM] Add a setting to turn variable refresh rate off

Variable refresh rate is used whenever the connector is vrr_capable. Add
"Variable refresh rate" to System / Display, shown when the display
supports it and on by default. Turning it off sends VRR_ENABLED 0 at the
next modeset and drops the VRR flag from the modes, so refresh rate
switches go back to the ordinary modes.

Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
